{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["And I say — Rabbi Moses said: <b>חָלִתִי</b> from the root as in <b>אֲשֶׁר חָלָה</b> (which YHWH ordained), like <b>עֲנֹתִי</b>; and the meaning of <b>שְׁנוֹת</b> is from the root of <b>שְׁנַת</b> עוֹלָם (eternal sleep). And this is far-fetched in my eyes, for how would the right hand, which is the arm, sleep?" "And others say: <b>כִּי שְׁנוֹת</b> — like <b>הִשְׁתַּנּוֹת</b>, from the root <b>שׁוֹנֶה</b>, distinct from every nation." "And the meaning of <b>יְמִין עֶלְיוֹן</b> — that the right hand is what wages war. And the meaning: <b>כִּי חָלִתִי</b> because the arm has changed, because its power is not seen in our exile. And others say: <b>כִּי חָלִתִי</b> from the root of <b>רַבִּים יְחַלּוּ פְּנֵי נָדִיב</b>, like <b>תְּפִלָּתִי</b>; and this root from this meaning is not found in all of Scripture except with the word פנים. And in my opinion: this is an allusion to the word <b>חָשַׁבְתִּי</b>, for thus it is — <b>חָשַׁבְתִּי</b>, a thought, and it is <b>חָלִתִי</b>, and it is the thought of <b>שְׁנוֹת יְמִין עֶלְיוֹן</b>, as he mentioned <b>שְׁנוֹת עוֹלָמִים</b>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 77, :notes {0 "Resolved ה' as YHWH per divine-name rule; the referent in the verse is the divine right hand.", 2 "שנות is polyvalent in this psalm; I have preserved each occurrence in Hebrew script since Ibn Ezra's argument turns on which root each interpreter assigns to it."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:57.984458243Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}